From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EvilMetaMonkey <hood.mj85@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 01:41:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Run CI tests with --concurrency=1

Five older test files set the process-wide Directory.current across async
gaps, which races when plain dart test runs files in parallel isolates of
one process (seen on PR #2 on macOS Intel and Windows). The documented
gate is dart test --concurrency=1; CI now runs the same command.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index b8efd9d725beff270fc98561c5789706fa7ad3fb..684f54c3a16ab602ba9cbd064addcff21449f3dd 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@ jobs:
           sdk: '3.11.5'
       - run: dart pub get --enforce-lockfile
       - run: dart run tool/check_analyzer.dart
-      - run: dart test
+      - run: dart test --concurrency=1
       - run: dart test tool/haven_contract_test.dart --concurrency=1
       - run: dart build cli -o build/ci-dmc
       - if: runner.os != 'Windows'
